🌟 Week 1 — Project Setup & Backend Integration
✅ What I Did

Set up the BragBoard project structure with frontend (React) and backend (FastAPI).

Installed and configured all dependencies for both frontend and backend.

Created basic API endpoints in FastAPI:

/register – Register a new user.

/login – Authenticate user and return JWT token.

/refresh – Refresh access token.

/me – Fetch logged-in user details.

/users – List all users.

/shoutouts – Create and fetch shoutouts.

Implemented JWT authentication to secure all protected routes.

Connected backend to the database to store users and shoutouts.

⚠️ Errors / Issues Faced

CORS Policy Error — React frontend couldn’t call FastAPI backend.

Solved by enabling CORS middleware in FastAPI.

Invalid Token Error — Token decoding failed during protected route access.

Fixed by properly decoding JWT using the secret key and checking token expiry.

Database Connection Error — Incorrect DB URL format.

Resolved by correcting connection string in .env.

🎯 Outcome

The backend API became fully functional and connected with the frontend, forming the foundation for authentication and data handling.

💻 Week 2 — Frontend Authentication & Dashboard Setup
✅ What I Did

Built the Login and Register pages using React and Tailwind CSS.

Integrated the frontend with backend APIs (/login and /register).

Stored the JWT token securely in localStorage.

Implemented route protection — if a user isn’t logged in, they’re redirected to the login page.

Designed and developed the Dashboard page layout:

Sidebar with navigation (Dashboard, Profile, Settings).

Main content area displaying a welcome message and shoutouts list.

Fetched user details from /me API and displayed the logged-in user’s name on the dashboard.

⚠️ Errors / Issues Faced

Token Missing in Headers — API calls failed due to missing authorization header.

Fixed by dynamically attaching Bearer ${token} in fetch requests.

Page Not Updating After Login — Used useNavigate incorrectly.

Solved by properly redirecting after setting token.

Dashboard Not Loading Data — Used incorrect endpoint names.

Corrected by using proper /me and /shoutouts routes.

🎯 Outcome

Users can now register, log in, and access the main dashboard with their personalized welcome message. Basic project flow is functional end-to-end.

🎉 Week 3 — Create a Shout-out Form with Recipient Tagging
✅ What I Did

Implemented the “Create Shout-out” form in the Dashboard.

Added recipient tagging (@mention) system:

Typing “@” shows a dropdown with user name suggestions from /users.

Selecting a user adds their name in the message and stores their ID in selectedRecipients.

Integrated the form with the /shoutouts POST API to save:

Message text

Department

Recipient IDs

Sender information

Automatically updated the “Recent Shoutouts” section after posting — no page refresh needed.

Enhanced UI using Tailwind CSS for a clean and interactive layout.

⚠️ Errors / Issues Faced

Mention Suggestions Not Showing

Cursor position and regex mismatch; fixed using selectionStart tracking.

Recipient IDs Not Saving in DB

Initially missing in payload; resolved by adding recipient_ids array in POST body.

Profile Showing Wrong Info

/me returned only name; fixed by updating frontend to handle full user data (name, email, department).

Token Expiry Errors (401)

Fixed by adding logout redirection if token is invalid.

UI Overlap for Mentions List

Solved using absolute positioning and z-index in Tailwind CSS.

🎯 Outcome

Shout-outs can now be created, tagged, and displayed dynamically. The Dashboard became interactive and user-friendly, meeting all Week 3 goals successfully. 🚀

