🌟 Week 5 — Add Reactions & Implement Reaction Counters with User Tracking

✅ What I Did

Added interactive Reactions (Like 👍, Clap 👏, and Star ⭐) feature for all shout-outs on the feed.

Implemented Reaction Counters for each post — dynamically displaying total counts beside every emoji.

Enabled User-Specific Reaction Tracking:

When a user clicks a reaction, it’s stored in the backend linked to both the user and shoutout.

The selected reaction turns blue, visually confirming the user’s response.

Users can toggle reactions on/off anytime.

Integrated the frontend with new backend APIs:

POST /reactions/{shoutout_id} — to add or toggle a user’s reaction.

GET /reactions/{shoutout_id} — to fetch all reactions and counts per post.

Enhanced the Shoutout Feed to show live updates:

Reaction counts and colors update instantly without reloading the page.

When navigating away and coming back, reactions persist based on saved user data.

Updated the models.py, schemas.py, and main.py to include:

Reaction model with foreign keys to both User and ShoutOut.

Logic to handle toggling (add/remove) reactions efficiently.

Aggregated counts per reaction type for each shoutout.

⚠️ Errors / Issues Faced

🔸 Reactions Not Persisting After Refresh

Initially, reactions didn’t save permanently.

Fixed by creating a dedicated Reaction model and linking it to User and ShoutOut.

🔸 Duplicate Reaction Entries

Multiple entries for same user + shoutout occurred.

Solved by adding a unique constraint and toggle mechanism in backend logic.

🔸 UI Not Updating Immediately

React state didn’t re-render after reacting.

Fixed by updating local state using setShoutouts() after each successful API response.

🔸 Count Mismatch Between Frontend and Backend

Counters weren’t syncing correctly.

Resolved by fetching updated reaction data after each toggle.

🎯 Outcome

Week 5 introduced social engagement to BragBoard 🎉
Users can now express appreciation for others’ shoutouts using reactions — making the platform more interactive and rewarding.

✨ The system accurately tracks each user’s reactions, updates counts in real-time, and ensures data consistency across frontend and backend.
